      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Logistical arguments often center on the impossibility of accurately tracing lineage and determining who qualifies as a direct descendant. Furthermore, opponents raise significant concerns about the sheer fiscal burden, arguing that the cost would be astronomical and necessitate massive tax increases. They also point to the lack of a clear, legally defined mechanism for such a massive, retroactive payment. These practical hurdles are used to dismiss the entire concept as an unworkable political fantasy.",
