      "content": "\"unworkable political fantasy\" is a pretty strong way to put it. do people who support reparations see those logistical issues as dealbreakers, or do they have ways to address them? like, is there a version of the debate where these practical points are actually addressed instead of just being used to shut the whole thing down?",
